    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 8,
        "sourceEnd": 292,
        "text": "Good evening. My name is Daniel Cho, and I work for the city planning office. Tonight I want to explain a new plan for the old market area. Some people support this plan, while others have concerns. I will describe both perspectives so that everyone understands the situation clearly.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "dd368051cfee015c81d34cef861bc92dd30d70ea0b5f088c0e5d301b079a52c8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leila",
        "speaker": "Leila",
        "sourceStart": 301,
        "sourceEnd": 371,
        "text": "Why is the work urgent rather than something we can leave until later?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "0cc0d5af0ea857ed6af2c1a795fdb7231baf77fc4344d1c2a8f4902fdaa3ecdb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 381,
        "sourceEnd": 888,
        "text": "The old market is located in the center of our city and is more than one hundred years old. Many small shops sell fruit, bread, and fish there. The buildings are beautiful but also old and weak. Last year, engineers inspected the roofs and found serious problems. Water comes through the roofs when it rains. The city must repair the market soon. The preservation of this historic area is important, but safety must come first. If we wait too long, the damage will only get worse and repairs will cost more.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "a8325fb99409d49fa81a2c8754d96691e1c748ee69d20bb01e88076889b7ea63",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "leila",
        "speaker": "Leila",
        "sourceStart": 897,
        "sourceEnd": 939,
        "text": "What exactly would change under this plan?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "281b36bfcbb39f1996e3739b46a24fd7e61aea82528c9c506433be7b0c594d87",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 949,
        "sourceEnd": 1391,
        "text": "Our plan has three parts. First, we will repair the old roofs using the same materials as before. This is essential for preservation, as the original look of the market will be maintained. Second, we will build a new covered walkway between the market and the bus station. This walkway will protect people from rain and sun. Third, we will add a small information center near the main entrance. The center will show the history of the market.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "6bb2e07a51b05f9e4b424d663b16f8232fb0cd8a3deee74ea70bea3393676b0a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "leila",
        "speaker": "Leila",
        "sourceStart": 1400,
        "sourceEnd": 1458,
        "text": "Do the people who use the market agree about the benefits?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "8870ff80ee8e1548e2a33595482d89108d1f79827979c481991f349351b06720",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1468,
        "sourceEnd": 2289,
        "text": "Now, some people say the plan is too big. A shop owner named Maria said, \"I like the repairs, but the new walkway will bring too many people. The market will become noisy.\" Another person, a teacher named Mr. Lee, said, \"I disagree. The walkway is good. More people will visit the market, and the shops will earn more money.\" These are both reasonable views, and we take them seriously. We understand that change can be difficult, but we believe the plan balances preservation with practical improvements. The walkway, for example, will be wide enough for people to pass comfortably, and it will be designed to fit the style of the old market. We have also considered Maria's concern about noise. The information center will help manage visitor numbers, and the city will monitor the situation after the work is finished.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "13f68bc96b36edc546ffcf968f9a932d4d234b2928ca9ea0dade3661d6968b5f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "leila",
        "speaker": "Leila",
        "sourceStart": 2298,
        "sourceEnd": 2372,
        "text": "And who will pay? Traders also need to know whether they can keep working.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "70a131f7edb187788879f209eb4aaddac42f99cb9552870c3b6b88e5002da77c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2382,
        "sourceEnd": 2889,
        "text": "The city will pay for the repairs. The new walkway will be paid for by a private company. The information center will be paid for by the city and the private company together. The work will start in March and finish in December. During the work, the market will stay open. However, some shops will move to a temporary area outside. The city engineer will supervise the work to ensure that the old structures are not damaged. The materials used for the repairs will match the original as closely as possible.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "70703a1333cc76cd07ffdff653a7ed8826271c5435e5cc2110e7a3c9a0a7be94",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "leila",
        "speaker": "Leila",
        "sourceStart": 2898,
        "sourceEnd": 3013,
        "text": "An information desk alone cannot control how many people arrive. How will you know whether the approach has worked?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "00b6d91f0076ee841ec51118bff709c42206b68bdd063642029cffce13dd00bc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 3023,
        "sourceEnd": 3334,
        "text": "Before construction, staff will count visitors and record noise at the same locations on market days. They will repeat those checks after the work is finished. Comparing equivalent days should help us separate changes linked to the walkway from a busy holiday, although it will not remove every other influence.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "452462808ebe7ad427451963b223379fcb37f36f8fd9ea1cd56b17e65def9e04",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "leila",
        "speaker": "Leila",
        "sourceStart": 3343,
        "sourceEnd": 3384,
        "text": "Where can residents question these plans?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "deac114f479d3dafdae8fd19dfd0bc46679c6385131f050737e168d8acb081a5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 3394,
        "sourceEnd": 3532,
        "text": "We will hold a public meeting next week. At the meeting, you can ask questions. You can also write to our office. Thank you for listening.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "ac5cb636a8c753b2f1a2bc9952e28f1ab425271178a4436e26b1516705180f23",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      }
    ]
  },
